Hi,

Below is an announcement of the recent minor update to PWG 5106.1
(abstract counters for all multifunction services), which corrects a bug
in the Media Used group of counters.

The SNMP binding of this specification (which also includes support
for subunits like Marker, Channel, etc.) is now under revision.  New
features are being added and a prototype by Samsung is now underway
(to finish by end-of-June).  Thus this MIB has been renamed from
Counter MIB v1 to Imaging System State and Counter MIB v2.

The latest working draft of the IS State and Counter MIB v2 is at:

  ftp://ftp.pwg.org/pub/pwg/wims/wd/wd-wimscountmib20-20070428.mib
    - ASN.1 only - compiles without warnings in Epilogue and SMICng

  ftp://ftp.pwg.org/pub/pwg/wims/wd/wd-wimscountmib20-20070428.pdf
    - PDF - color-highlighted ASN.1 of MIB

Cheers,
- Ira

